00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:17,243
The call There is a shelf of part-used
concentrates: a weed killer bought for one

64
00:01:17,243 --> 00:01:17,486
path, a rooting hormone, a bug spray whose
label has washed to nothing.

65
00:01:17,486 --> 00:01:17,729
You avoid this shelf because there is no
easy way to get rid of them, and pouring

66
00:01:17,729 --> 00:01:17,971
them down a drain is not one.

67
00:01:17,971 --> 00:01:18,214
Two rules settle it.

68
00:01:18,214 --> 00:01:18,457
First, if you cannot read the label, that
container is finished, no exceptions,

69
00:01:18,457 --> 00:01:18,700
because an unlabelled garden chemical
cannot be used safely by you or by anyone
who

70
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:18,943
finds it later; it goes to the household
hazardous waste collection.

71
00:01:18,943 --> 00:01:19,186
Second, if you can read it, ask whether
you have used it in the last two growing

72
00:01:19,186 --> 00:01:19,429
seasons.

73
00:01:19,429 --> 00:01:19,671
If not, it goes the same way.

74
00:01:19,671 --> 00:01:19,914
What survives is a short row you can name
from the doorway.

